From a7cd6c952d53159140fd6cda06c0e66b8674ee84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Blumenkrantz <michael.blumenkrantz@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 11:20:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] zink: share bindless handles between contexts

bindless handles belong to the share group, but zink allocated them and
looked them up per context, so a handle made resident or deleted in any
context other than the one which created it hit an assert or used
another context's descriptor with the same id

move the slot allocators and handle tables to the screen, and refcount
the descriptors so the creating handle and each residency keep them
alive until the batches using them are done

Fixes: bc202553e9b7 ("zink: implement bindless textures")
Generated-by: LLM
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45450>
